<p>I still find that assuming the intervals are random isn't actually supported here. I think you want &quot;unpredictable intervals&quot; or &quot;based on currently unknown variables&quot; or something. AFAICT, there's no reason that the Foundation would have to assume a statistically random process as more likely than one based on variables that aren't known to them. It <em>could</em> be random, but it also could not be, and given that very few things in reality are actually random, it probably isn't.</p>

